<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Man Mandir Palace</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Man Mandir Palace stands inside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwalior-fort">Gwalior Fort</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and was built by the Tomara king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/man-singh-tomar">Man Singh Tomar</a> between about 1486 and 1516. Its outer walls are decorated with bands of blue, green and yellow glazed tiles showing ducks, elephants, tigers and plantain trees, and it has several underground storeys. It is one of the finest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> palaces of its time and influenced later Mughal palace building.</p></div>
